From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:07:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 279/333] [ae-patch] Let a queued Compact run while background
 shells are still running

The queued Compact (the rail's Context button and the action dock's Compact
card) only advanced when the session was idle with no background shell. A
claude-native chat ends a turn as `waiting` while a background shell still
runs, and the page's shell tally stays sticky until the next Stop hook, so a
lead chat with a CI wait or watcher running kept its Compact queued forever.

safeNow() now treats `waiting` like `idle` and no longer looks at background
shells: they outlive turns, survive /compact, and the TUI accepts /compact
while they run. A streaming turn, any other session status and a queued
message for the chat still hold the plan back. The tests that pinned the old
rule now assert those are safe points, and a regression test drives the real
store reducer through a claude-native turn end with a shell still running
(2026-11-01).
